{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Structures","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Structures","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.adjoint_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.adjoint_dim","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L133-L134","doc":"The adjoint object has spin `1` and dimension `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.fundamental_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.fundamental_dim","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L130-L131","doc":"The fundamental object has spin `1/2` and dimension `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.cat_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.cat_dim","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L128-L128","doc":"The categorical dimension of `V_j` is `2j + 1 = twice_j + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.twice_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.twice_j","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L126-L126","doc":"The spin label `j`, represented as twice the spin (so `j = 0, 1, 2, 3, ...`\ncorresponds to spin `0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, ...`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels","kind":"structure","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L118-L128","doc":"**Spin labels**: the simple objects of a quantum observable universe\nare indexed by half-integer spin labels `j ∈ {0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, ...}`,\nwith `V_j` having categorical dimension `2j + 1`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:spin-labels}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IsAntiSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IsAntiSelfDual","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L113-L116","doc":"An element `v : V` is **anti-self-dual** if `⋆(v) = -v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L108-L111","doc":"An element `v : V` is **self-dual** if `⋆(v) = v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.star_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.star_sq","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L106-L106","doc":"Involutivity: `⋆(⋆(v)) = v` for all `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.star","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The Hodge star `⋆ : V → V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution","kind":"structure","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L100-L106","doc":"An **involution on a type** (concrete version for the ℂ realisation).\nModels the Hodge star acting pointwise on sections of a bundle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L94-L98","doc":"A morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` is **self-dual** w.r.t. a categorical Hodge\ninvolution if `f ≫ ⋆ = f`, i.e. `f` lands in the `+1`-eigenspace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star_sq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L92-L92","doc":"Involutivity: `⋆ ≫ ⋆ = id_X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The Hodge star operator `⋆ : X ⟶ X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution","kind":"structure","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L83-L92","doc":"An **involutive endomorphism** in a category, modeling the Hodge star\noperator `⋆`.  When `⋆² = id`, the eigenvalue decomposition\n`V = V⁺ ⊕ V⁻` (self-dual ⊕ anti-self-dual) follows from the spectral\ntheory of involutions. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-hodge-star","label":"def:categorical-hodge-star","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure.positive_definite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure.positive_definite","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Positive-definiteness: for non-zero `f : 𝟙 → X`, `f ≫ f† ≠ 0`.\n(In an ℝ-linear category, this encodes positivity.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure.toInvolutiveStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure.toInvolutiveStructure","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L71-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PositiveDefiniteStructure","kind":"structure","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L64-L79","doc":"**Positive-definite structure** on an involutive monoidal category.\n\nThe involution is positive-definite if for every non-zero\n`f : 𝟙 → X`, the composite `f ≫ f† : 𝟙 → 𝟙` is positive\nin `End(𝟙) ≅ R`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:positive-definite-dagger}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.involutivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.involutivity","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L57-L62","doc":"`f†† = f` is the defining involutivity property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger_id","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Identity: `id† = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger_comp","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Contravariance: `(g ∘ f)† = f† ∘ g†`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger_dagger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger_dagger","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Involutivity: `f†† = f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InvolutiveStructure.dagger","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The involution on morphisms: `f† : Y ⟶ X` for `f : X ⟶ Y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InvolutiveStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InvolutiveStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InvolutiveStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InvolutiveStructure","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L39-L55","doc":"**Involutive structure** (†-structure / *-structure) on a monoidal category.\n\nA contravariant endofunctor `† : C^op → C` that is the identity on objects,\nsatisfies `f†† = f`, and is compatible with the monoidal structure.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:involutive-structure}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:involutive-structure","label":"def:involutive-structure","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/involutive-structure.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HigherForms.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HigherForms.d","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The differential `d : Ωᵏ(A) → Ωᵏ⁺¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HigherForms.degree_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HigherForms.degree_zero","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L35-L35","doc":"`Ω⁰(A) = A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HigherForms.formObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HigherForms.formObj","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The degree-`k` form object `Ωᵏ(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HigherForms.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HigherForms.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L31-L31","doc":"The underlying Frobenius–Hopf object `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HigherForms.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HigherForms.mk","kind":"ctor","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HigherForms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HigherForms","kind":"structure","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Structures.lean#L22-L37","doc":"**Higher differential forms** `Ωᵏ(A) = ⋀ᵏ_A Ω¹(A)`.\n\nThe graded `A`-bimodule of exterior powers of Kähler differentials,\nwith `Ω⁰(A) = A` and `d : Ωᵏ → Ωᵏ⁺¹` satisfying `d² = 0`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:higher-forms}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:higher-forms","label":"def:higher-forms","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/higher-forms.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}